meta {
  name: Resolve Deal Audit Item
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/deal-audits/{{dealAuditItemId}}/resolve
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "note": "Verified prior insurance proof with the client.",
    "attachment": {
      "key": "{{dealAuditAttachmentKey}}",
      "filename": "prior-insurance.pdf",
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "size": 2048
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the resolved item", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("id");
    expect(body).to.have.property("resolved");
    expect(body.resolved).to.equal(true);
    expect(body).to.have.property("resolvedAt");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /deal-audits/:itemId/resolve — resolve a hand-off item (PAC-14)

  Marks a pending service hand-off audit item as **verified/complete** so it
  drops off the "Deals Pending Service Hand-off" board. Optionally records a
  note and/or a supporting document (uploaded first via **Presign Audit
  Attachment**). Writes an `audit_resolved` **activity** (who/when) for the
  timeline.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits`
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:write` (`write ⇒ read`)
  - **Data scope:** a producer (`own`) may only resolve their **own** items
    (`producerId = user`); branch callers are limited to their branch. Resolving
    another producer's item is rejected by the guard/service (`403`).

  Effect: sets `updateStatus = "complete"` (`Verified - Complete`),
  `isResolved = true`, `resolvedAt`, `resolvedById`, and appends any attachment.

  **Idempotent.** Resolving is one-shot: if the item is already resolved the call
  returns `200` with the *original* `resolvedAt` and changes nothing — a replay
  (stale tab, client retry) will not append the attachment or overwrite the note
  a second time.

  The `audit_resolved` activity is written **best-effort** after the item is
  committed: if the timeline write fails it is logged server-side, but the call
  still reports success because the resolution itself has already been applied.

  ## Path params
  | param  | type   | notes                          |
  |--------|--------|--------------------------------|
  | itemId | string | Deal Audit Item `_id` (raw id) |

  ## Body (all optional)
  | field      | type   | rules                                              |
  |------------|--------|----------------------------------------------------|
  | note       | string | ≤ 2000 chars                                       |
  | attachment | object | `{ key, filename, contentType, size }` from presign |

  `attachment.key` **must** be a key returned by the presign endpoint and the
  object must already exist in storage (the upload completed), else `404`.

  ### A document requirement needs its document (PAC-106)

  An item whose template says `requiresUpload` (Good Student, Prior Insurance,
  Accord Cancellation, Defensive Driver, Fire Subscription, Hail Resistant
  Roof — the board row's `requiresUpload: true`) cannot be resolved without a
  file: `400` unless the body carries an `attachment` or the item already has
  one on file. A yes/no requirement (Inspection, Actual Cash Value,
  Mortgagee) still resolves with a note alone.

  Resolving is the producer's *claim*; the manager's verdict on the Deal Audit
  page (**Set Item Verdict**) is the *verification*, and the only thing the
  Approve gate reads.

  ```json
  {
    "note": "Uploaded the signed defensive-driver certificate.",
    "attachment": {
      "key": "agencies/<agencyId>/deal-audits/<itemId>/<uuid>-cert.pdf",
      "filename": "cert.pdf",
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "size": 204800
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "id": "665f...ac1", "resolved": true, "resolvedAt": "2026-07-23T12:00:00.000Z" }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — invalid body (note too long, bad attachment metadata),
    or a `requiresUpload` item with no document.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — module disabled, missing `deal_audits:write`, or the item
    is not the caller's (own scope) / not in their branch.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such audit item, or the declared attachment object was
    not found in storage.
}
